{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-5-20251101","id":"msg_014NX5y1Syc1mtxfmRJM2nFm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────\n**Critical Issue Found**: `YellowDog.Dhcpv6.Handler` doesn't implement `child_spec/1` which the Abyss connection supervisor needs. The other handlers (DHCPv4, mDNS) likely have this since they work, but DHCPv6 is missing it.\n\n**Root Cause**: When Abyss tries to start a handler for a new UDP packet, it treats the handler module as a child spec, but `YellowDog.Dhcpv6.Handler` is just a module with callback functions, not a GenServer that defines `child_spec/1`.\n─────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\nLet me examine the DHCPv6 handler and compare it with the working handlers."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5242,"cache_read_input_tokens":57254,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":5242,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"50d21925-9237-40c9-8dd2-03e5c6e35c37","uuid":"1db5dc60-cecc-4475-a8fe-5e3848b1184b"}
