(80c73c1)\n    69→  - ACL evaluation in DISCOVER handling (allow/deny/custom_options)\n    70→  - ConflictResolver integration in DECLINE handling\n    71→  - CustomOptions template substitution in responses\n    72→- [x] Added handler integration tests (68c77b3)\n    73→  - DECLINE triggers ConflictResolver\n    74→  - IP quarantine verification\n    75→  - Conflict stats tracking\n    76→- [x] Fixed format_mac to handle 16-byte chaddr field\n    77→- [x] All 105 DHCPv4 tests pass, 1314 tests across all apps\n    78→\n    79→### Completed (Iteration 4 - Test Quality)\n    80→- [x] Reduced test log noise from expected error behaviors\n    81→  - DNS zone auth: Changed to debug level for \"No zone file path configured\"\n    82→  - ZoneService: Added suppress function for expected save errors\n    83→  - Added `@tag :capture_log` to tests that intentionally trigger errors:\n    84→    - `conflict_resolver_test.exs` - conflict handling tests\n    85→    - `handler_test.exs` (DHCPv4) - DECLINE handling tests\n    86→    - `handler_test.exs` (DNS) - error handling tests\n    87→    - `config_test.exs` - missing file and malformed TOML tests\n    88→    - `integration_test.exs` - error recovery tests\n    89→    - `config_manager_test.exs` - file not found tests\n    90→    - `settings_live_test.exs` - missing configuration tests\n    91→- [x] All 335+ tests pass with clean output (96c582d)\n    92→\n    93→### Completed (Iteration 5 - Security: Web Console Authentication)\n    94→- [x] Created `YellowDog.Console.Plugs.BasicAuth` module (b32bbd7)\n    95→  - Environment-based configuration (CONSOLE_USERNAME, CONSOLE_PASSWORD)\n    96→  - Constant-time string comparison to prevent timing attacks\n    97→  - Graceful degradation when password not configured (with warning log)\n    98→  - Configurable realm for WWW-Authenticate header\n    99→- [x] Added plug to browser pipeline in router.ex\n   100→- [x] Configured authentication per environment:\n   101→  - Disabled by default in dev (set CONSOLE_AUTH_ENABLED=true to enable)\n   102→  - Disabled by default in test (for automated testing)\n   103→  - Enabled by default in production (requires CONSOLE_PASSWORD env var)\n   104→- [x] Added comprehensive unit tests (14 tests)\n   105→- [x] All 177 tests pass\n   106→\n   107→### Completed (Iteration 6 - Security: DHCP Rate Limiting)\n   108→- [x] Created `YellowDog.Dhcpv4.RateLimiter` module (e8f5f5e)\n   109→  - Token bucket algorithm for per-client and global rate limiting\n   110→  - Configurable burst capacity and refill rates\n   111→  - ETS-based storage for high-performance bucket tracking\n   112→  - Automatic cleanup of expired client buckets\n   113→  - Telemetry events for monitoring rate limit violations\n   114→- [x] Integrated rate limiter with DHCPv4 handler\n   115→  - Rate check before processing any DHCP message\n   116→  - Silent drop of rate-limited requests (per RFC)\n   117→- [x] Added RateLimiter to supervisor child list\n   118→- [x] Added comprehensive unit tests (16 tests)\n   119→- [x] All 121 tests pass (7 excluded)\n   120→\n   121→### Completed (Iteration 7 - DHCPv6 Rate Limiting)\n   122→- [x] Verified DNS compression loop protection is already implemented\n   123→  - `DNS.Message.Domain` has loop detection via visited positions MapSet\n   124→  - Max compression depth limiting (5 levels)\n   125→  - Comprehensive security tests in `dns/security_test.exs`\n   126→- [x] Created `YellowDog.Dhcpv6.RateLimiter` module (b1096df)\n   127→  - Token bucket algorithm for per-client and global rate limiting\n   128→  - ETS-based storage for high-performance bucket tracking\n   129→  - Configurable burst capacity and refill rates\n   130→  - Automatic cleanup of expired client buckets\n   131→  - Telemetry events for monitoring rate limit violations\n   132→  - Graceful handling when not running\n   133→- [x] Integrated rate limiter with DHCPv6 handler\n   134→  - Rate check before processing any DHCPv6 message\n   135→  - Silent drop of rate-limited requests (per RFC)\n   136→- [x] Added RateLimiter to supervisor child list\n   137→- [x] Added comprehensive unit tests (16 tests)\n   138→- [x] All tests pass (734 tests, excluding integration)\n   139→\n   140→### Completed (Iteration 8 - DNS Rate Limiting)\n   141→- [x] Created `YellowDog.Dns.RateLimiter` module (a0fcd2b)\n   142→  - Token bucket algorithm for per-client and global rate limiting\n   143→  - Higher defaults for DNS (50 client tokens, 5000 global vs 10/1000 DHCP)\n   144→  - ETS-based storage for high-performance bucket tracking\n   145→  - Configurable burst capacity and refill rates (20/sec vs 2/sec for DHCP)\n   146→  - Automatic cleanup of expired client buckets\n   147→  - Telemetry events for monitoring rate limit violations\n   148→  - Graceful handling when not running\n   149→- [x] Integrated rate limiter with DNS UDP handler\n   150→  - Rate check before processing any DNS message\n   151→  - Silent drop of rate-limited requests (per RFC best practices)\n   152→- [x] Added RateLimiter to supervisor child list\n   153→- [x] Added comprehensive unit tests (17 tests)\n   154→- [x] All tests pass (751 tests, excluding integration)\n   155→\n   156→### In Progress\n   157→- [ ] Performance optimization review\n   158→\n   159→### Known Issues (Documented but not fixed)\n   160→1. ~~**CRITICAL**: Web console has NO authentication~~ **FIXED (b32bbd7)**\n   161→2. ~~**HIGH**: DHCP lease allocation has no rate limiting~~ **FIXED (e8f5f5e, b1096df)**\n   162→3. ~~**MEDIUM**: DNS compression loop vulnerability~~ **ALREADY MITIGATED in ex_dns**\n   163→4. ~~**MEDIUM**: DNS server has no rate limiting~~ **FIXED (a0fcd2b)**\n   164→\n   165→### Next Steps\n   166→1. Performance profiling of DNS/DHCP handlers\n   167→2. Consider adding rate limiting to mDNS server\n   168→3. Investigate further security hardening opportunities\n   169→\n   170→## Key Findings\n   171→\n   172→### DHCPv6 Handler Bug (FIXED - Iteration 2)\n   173→- Location: `apps/yellow_dog_dhcpv6/lib/yellow_dog/dhcpv6/handler.ex`\n   174→- Issue: Missing `use Abyss.Handler` macro, causing child_spec/1 error\n   175→- Fix: Added `use Abyss.Handler` and `@impl true` annotations\n   176→\n   177→### Abyss Listener Blocking (FIXED - Iteration 2)\n   178→- Location: `apps/abyss/lib/abyss/listener.ex`\n   179→- Issue: `transport.recv(socket, 0, :infinity)` blocked GenServer calls\n   180→- Fix: Changed to `recv(socket, 0, 100)` with retry loop for responsiveness\n   181→\n   182→### Console Config Validation (FIXED - Iteration 2)\n   183→- Location: `config/test.exs`\n   184→- Issue: `code_reloader` set at compile time in dev.exs but missing in test config\n   185→- Fix: Added `code_reloader: false` to test endpoint config\n   186→\n   187→### Security Improvements (Iteration 2)\n   188→1. DNS UDP handler: Added try-rescue for exception handling\n   189→2. DHCPv4: Replaced silent fallback with logging for ip_to_binary\n   190→3. DHCPv6: Added DNS label length validation (max 63 bytes per RFC 1035)\n   191→\n   192→## Mistakes & Learnings\n   193→1. **Umbrella dependency order matters**: When one umbrella app uses modules from another, it must declare the dependency explicitly.\n   194→2. **UDP server tests can be flaky**: Tests involving UDP servers with blocking recv calls can timeout - better to mark as integration tests.\n   195→3. **Handler modules need proper macros**: Protocol handler modules (like DHCPv6) need `use Abyss.Handler` to be supervised correctly.\n   196→4. **Blocking recv prevents GenServer responsiveness**: GenServer calls timeout if the process is blocked in recv(:infinity). Use timeouts with retry.\n   197→5. **Compile-time config needs runtime match**: Phoenix endpoints with compile-time config (like code_reloader) need matching runtime config in all environments.\n   198→6. **Silent fallbacks mask bugs**: Functions like ip_to_binary should log errors instead of silently using default values.\n   199→7. **RFC compliance matters**: DNS labels must be ≤63 bytes; validation prevents buffer issues.\n   200→\n   201→## Architecture Notes\n   202→- 11-app umbrella project\n   203→- Core services: DNS, mDNS, DHCPv4, DHCPv6\n   204→- Infrastructure libs: abyss (UDP), ex_dns (DNS protocol), ex_dhcp (DHCP protocol), geo_ip_db (IP geolocation)\n   205→- Web console: Phoenix LiveView with DaisyUI\n   206→\n   207→### PRD Implementation Modules\n   208→\n   209→**New Modules Created**:\n   210→1. `apps/yellow_dog_dhcpv4/lib/yellow_dog/dhcpv4/pool_config.ex`\n   211→   - TOML pool configuration parsing and validation\n   212→   - Subnet mask calculation from CIDR notation\n   213→   - Range and reservation conversion\n   214→\n   215→2. `apps/yellow_dog_dhcpv4/lib/yellow_dog/dhcpv4/acl.ex`\n   216→   - ACL rule validation and evaluation\n   217→   - Pattern matching (glob support for MAC addresses)\n   218→   - Priority-based rule ordering\n   219→\n   220→3. `apps/yellow_dog_dhcpv4/lib/yellow_dog/dhcpv4/conflict_resolver.ex`\n   221→   - GenServer for IP conflict management\n   222→   - Quarantine tracking with expiration\n   223→   - Integration with LeaseManager for reassignment\n   224→\n   225→4. `apps/yellow_dog_dhcpv4/lib/yellow_dog/dhcpv4/custom_options.ex`\n   226→   - DHCP option validation by type\n   227→   - Template variable substitution\n   228→   - Binary encoding for packet generation\n   229→\n   230→**Modified Modules**:\n   231→- `apps/yellow_dog_dhcpv4/lib/yellow_dog/dhcpv4/lease_manager.ex`\n   232→  - Fixed bugs in `get_pool_config` and `get_static_reservations` handlers\n   233→  - Changed from Map.get to Enum.find (pools stored as list)\n   234→  - Return full pool struct instead of partial config\n   235→\n   236→- `apps/yellow_dog_dhcpv4/lib/yellow_dog/dhcpv4/handler.ex`\n   237→  - ACL evaluation before lease allocation\n   238→  - ConflictResolver integration for DECLINE\n   239→  - CustomOptions support with template substitution\n   240→  