{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nAnalysis:\nLet me analyze this conversation chronologically to capture all the important details:\n\n1. **Initial Context**: This is a continuation of a previous conversation (Loki Mode - autonomous improvement loop). The summary from the previous session shows:\n   - YellowDog project - Elixir umbrella project with DNS, mDNS, DHCPv4, DHCPv6 services\n   - Previous iterations completed security improvements including web console auth and DHCPv4 rate limiting\n   - Last commit was e8f5f5e for DHCPv4 rate limiting\n   - Known issues identified: CRITICAL (web console auth - fixed), HIGH (DHCP rate limiting - fixed), MEDIUM (DNS compression loop)\n\n2. **Current Session Work**:\n\n   a. **First Task - Verify DNS compression loop protection**:\n   - Read `DNS.Message.Domain` module to verify loop detection\n   - Found it already implements loop detection via MapSet tracking visited positions\n   - Max compression depth limiting (5 levels)\n   - Comprehensive security tests in `dns/security_test.exs`\n   - Marked as ALREADY MITIGATED\n\n   b. **Second Task - DHCPv6 Rate Limiting**:\n   - Created `YellowDog.Dhcpv6.RateLimiter` module\n   - Integrated with DHCPv6 handler\n   - Added to supervisor child list\n   - Created 16 tests - all pass\n   - Committed as b1096df\n\n   c. **Third Task - DNS Rate Limiting**:\n   - Created `YellowDog.Dns.RateLimiter` module\n   - Higher defaults for DNS (50 client tokens, 5000 global vs 10/1000 DHCP)\n   - Integrated with DNS UDP handler\n   - Added to supervisor child list\n   - Created 17 tests - all pass\n   - Committed as a0fcd2b\n\n   d. **Fourth Task - mDNS Rate Limiting**:\n   - Created `YellowDog.Mdns.RateLimiter` module\n   - Higher defaults for mDNS (100 source tokens, 10000 global)\n   - Integrated with