{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01A1w2LzjMP8fsiMSWkeJrXx","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→defmodule YellowDog.Console.ServiceManager do\n     2→  @moduledoc \"\"\"\n     3→  Manages service lifecycle operations for web console.\n     4→\n     5→  Provides safe restart mechanisms with configuration updates using OTP\n     6→  supervisor terminate-and-restart pattern.\n     7→\n     8→  Based on research findings from research.md:\n     9→  - Update configuration in YellowDog.Config Agent\n    10→  - Terminate supervisor (OTP restarts automatically)\n    11→  - Monitor for restart completion\n    12→  - Verify service health\n    13→  \"\"\"\n    14→\n    15→  @doc \"\"\"\n    16→  Applies pending configuration for a service and restarts it.\n    17→\n    18→  ## Steps\n    19→    1. Update configuration in YellowDog.Config Agent\n    20→    2. Get current supervisor PID for service\n    21→    3. Terminate supervisor (OTP will restart automatically)\n    22→    4. Monitor for restart completion\n    23→    5. Verify service health\n    24→\n    25→  ## Parameters\n    26→    - service: Service atom (:dns, :mdns, :dhcpv4, :dhcpv6)\n    27→    - new_config: Map of new configuration values\n    28→\n    29→  ## Returns\n    30→    - `:ok` if successful\n    31→    - `{:error, reason}` if restart failed\n    32→\n    33→  ## Examples\n    34→\n    35→      iex> new_config = %{enabled: true, listen: \"0.0.0.0\", port: 5353}\n    36→      iex> ServiceManager.apply_and_restart(:dns, new_config)\n    37→      :ok\n    38→  \"\"\"\n    39→  @spec apply_and_restart(atom(), map()) :: :ok | {:error, term()}\n    40→  def apply_and_restart(service, new_config) do\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_017aewAbAZ8fZWMahUzBSjcc","session_id":"0d3ee750-7f11-4e1e-a617-3b37d644afe9","uuid":"e8a4ab0d-26ff-4a0a-af61-8da73964ca97","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/gao/Workspace/gsmlg-dev/yellow-dog/apps/yellow_dog_console/lib/yellow_dog/console/service_manager.ex","content":"defmodule YellowDog.Console.ServiceManager do\n  @moduledoc \"\"\"\n  Manages service lifecycle operations for web console.\n\n  Provides safe restart mechanisms with configuration updates using OTP\n  supervisor terminate-and-restart pattern.\n\n  Based on research findings from research.md:\n  - Update configuration in YellowDog.Config Agent\n  - Terminate supervisor (OTP restarts automatically)\n  - Monitor for restart completion\n  - Verify service health\n  \"\"\"\n\n  @doc \"\"\"\n  Applies pending configuration for a service and restarts it.\n\n  ## Steps\n    1. Update configuration in YellowDog.Config Agent\n    2. Get current supervisor PID for service\n    3. Terminate supervisor (OTP will restart automatically)\n    4. Monitor for restart completion\n    5. Verify service health\n\n  ## Parameters\n    - service: Service atom (:dns, :mdns, :dhcpv4, :dhcpv6)\n    - new_config: Map of new configuration values\n\n  ## Returns\n    - `:ok` if successful\n    - `{:error, reason}` if restart failed\n\n  ## Examples\n\n      iex> new_config = %{enabled: true, listen: \"0.0.0.0\", port: 5353}\n      iex> ServiceManager.apply_and_restart(:dns, new_config)\n      :ok\n  \"\"\"\n  @spec apply_and_restart(atom(), map()) :: :ok | {:error, term()}\n  def apply_and_restart(service, new_config) do","numLines":40,"startLine":1,"totalLines":281}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MdSqp4tWhEFTHiysk3LyhX","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→defmodule YellowDog.Console.LogBroadcaster do\n     2→  @moduledoc \"\"\"\n     3→  Broadcasts telemetry log events to connected LiveView processes via PubSub.\n     4→\n     5→  This GenServer attaches to all log-level telemetry events (debug, info, warning, error)\n     6→  and broadcasts them to the \"logs:stream\" PubSub topic. LiveView processes can subscribe\n     7→  to this topic to receive real-time log updates.\n     8→\n     9→  ## Usage\n    10→\n    11→  Start the broadcaster as part of the Console application supervisor:\n    12→\n    13→      children = [\n    14→        YellowDog.Console.LogBroadcaster,\n    15→        # ...\n    16→      ]\n    17→\n    18→  LiveViews subscribe in mount/3:\n    19→\n    20→      def mount(_params, _session, socket) do\n    21→        if connected?(socket) do\n    22→          Phoenix.PubSub.subscribe(YellowDog.Console.PubSub, \"logs:stream\")\n    23→        end\n    24→        {:ok, socket}\n    25→      end\n    26→\n    27→  And receive events in handle_info/2:\n    28→\n    29→      def handle_info({:log_event, level, measurements, metadata}, socket) do\n    30→        # Process the log event\n    31→        {:noreply, socket}\n    32→      end\n    33→  \"\"\"\n    34→\n    35→  use GenServer\n    36→\n    37→  @pubsub YellowDog.Console.PubSub\n    38→  @topic \"logs:stream\"\n    39→\n    40→  @doc \"\"\"\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_017aewAbAZ8fZWMahUzBSjcc","session_id":"0d3ee750-7f11-4e1e-a617-3b37d644afe9","uuid":"5401cd49-dc89-4959-9aa0-a5121c88b717","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/gao/Workspace/gsmlg-dev/yellow-dog/apps/yellow_dog_console/lib/yellow_dog/console/log_broadcaster.ex","content":"defmodule YellowDog.Console.LogBroadcaster do\n  @moduledoc \"\"\"\n  Broadcasts telemetry log events to connected LiveView processes via PubSub.\n\n  This GenServer attaches to all log-level telemetry events (debug, info, warning, error)\n  and broadcasts them to the \"logs:stream\" PubSub topic. LiveView processes can subscribe\n  to this topic to receive real-time log updates.\n\n  ## Usage\n\n  Start the broadcaster as part of the Console application supervisor:\n\n      children = [\n        YellowDog.Console.LogBroadcaster,\n        # ...\n      ]\n\n  LiveViews subscribe in mount/3:\n\n      def mount(_params, _session, socket) do\n        if connected?(socket) do\n          Phoenix.PubSub.subscribe(YellowDog.Console.PubSub, \"logs:stream\")\n        end\n        {:ok, socket}\n      end\n\n  And receive events in handle_info/2:\n\n      def handle_info({:log_event, level, measurements, metadata}, socket) do\n        # Process the log event\n        {:noreply, socket}\n      end\n  \"\"\"\n\n  use GenServer\n\n  @pubsub YellowDog.Console.PubSub\n  @topic \"logs:stream\"\n\n  @doc \"\"\"","numLines":40,"startLine":1,"totalLines":86}}}
