{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NhyNa3JrMnhMcrA6z4Jtpv","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→defmodule YellowDog.Dhcpv4.LeaseStorage do\n     2→  @moduledoc \"\"\"\n     3→  Persistent lease storage using Mnesia.\n     4→\n     5→  Provides a durable, transactional storage layer for DHCP leases with\n     6→  support for multiple lease states and comprehensive querying.\n     7→\n     8→  ## Lease States\n     9→\n    10→  - `:offered` - IP address offered to client, awaiting REQUEST\n    11→  - `:active` - Lease active and in use by client\n    12→  - `:released` - Client released the lease voluntarily\n    13→  - `:expired` - Lease exceeded its lifetime\n    14→  - `:declined` - Client declined the offered IP (conflict detected)\n    15→\n    16→  ## Storage Modes\n    17→\n    18→  - `:disc_copies` - Persistent storage (default for production)\n    19→  - `:ram_copies` - Memory-only storage (for testing)\n    20→  \"\"\"\n    21→\n    22→  require Record\n    23→\n    24→  alias YellowDog.Dhcpv4.AddressPool\n    25→\n    26→  @type ip_address :: AddressPool.ip_address()\n    27→  @type mac_address :: binary()\n    28→  @type client_id :: binary() | nil\n    29→  @type lease_state :: :offered | :active | :released | :expired | :declined\n    30→\n    31→  @type lease :: %{\n    32→          mac_address: mac_address(),\n    33→          ip_address: ip_address(),\n    34→          pool_name: String.t(),\n    35→          state: lease_state(),\n    36→          lease_time: pos_integer(),\n    37→          expires_at: integer(),\n    38→          hostname: String.t() | nil,\n    39→          client_id: client_id(),\n    40→          created_at: integer(),\n    41→          updated_at: integer()\n    42→        }\n    43→\n    44→  # Define Mnesia record\n    45→  Record.defrecord(:lease_record,\n    46→    mac_address: nil,\n    47→    ip_address: nil,\n    48→    pool_name: nil,\n    49→    state: :offered,\n    50→    lease_time: 0,\n    51→    expires_at: 0,\n    52→    hostname: nil,\n    53→    client_id: nil,\n    54→    created_at: 0,\n    55→    updated_at: 0\n    56→  )\n    57→\n    58→  @table_name :dhcpv4_leases\n    59→\n    60→  ## Public API\n    61→\n    62→  @doc \"\"\"\n    63→  Initializes the Mnesia schema and creates the leases table.\n    64→\n    65→  ## Options\n    66→\n    67→  - `:storage_type` - `:disc_copies` (default) or `:ram_copies`\n    68→  - `:nodes` - List of nodes to create table on (default: [node()])\n    69→\n    70→  ## Returns\n    71→\n    72→  - `:ok` - Successfully initialized\n    73→  - `{:error, reason}` - Failed to initialize\n    74→  \"\"\"\n    75→  @spec init(keyword()) :: :ok | {:error, term()}\n    76→  def init(opts \\\\ []) do\n    77→    storage_type = Keyword.get(opts, :storage_type, :disc_copies)\n    78→    nodes = Keyword.get(opts, :nodes, [node()])\n    79→\n    80→    with :ok <- ensure_schema_created(nodes),\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0d3ee750-7f11-4e1e-a617-3b37d644afe9","uuid":"1450ed52-4da7-40b9-a597-b74f13a1b4cf","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/gao/Workspace/gsmlg-dev/yellow-dog/apps/yellow_dog_dhcpv4/lib/yellow_dog/dhcpv4/lease_storage.ex","content":"defmodule YellowDog.Dhcpv4.LeaseStorage do\n  @moduledoc \"\"\"\n  Persistent lease storage using Mnesia.\n\n  Provides a durable, transactional storage layer for DHCP leases with\n  support for multiple lease states and comprehensive querying.\n\n  ## Lease States\n\n  - `:offered` - IP address offered to client, awaiting REQUEST\n  - `:active` - Lease active and in use by client\n  - `:released` - Client released the lease voluntarily\n  - `:expired` - Lease exceeded its lifetime\n  - `:declined` - Client declined the offered IP (conflict detected)\n\n  ## Storage Modes\n\n  - `:disc_copies` - Persistent storage (default for production)\n  - `:ram_copies` - Memory-only storage (for testing)\n  \"\"\"\n\n  require Record\n\n  alias YellowDog.Dhcpv4.AddressPool\n\n  @type ip_address :: AddressPool.ip_address()\n  @type mac_address :: binary()\n  @type client_id :: binary() | nil\n  @type lease_state :: :offered | :active | :released | :expired | :declined\n\n  @type lease :: %{\n          mac_address: mac_address(),\n          ip_address: ip_address(),\n          pool_name: String.t(),\n          state: lease_state(),\n          lease_time: pos_integer(),\n          expires_at: integer(),\n          hostname: String.t() | nil,\n          client_id: client_id(),\n          created_at: integer(),\n          updated_at: integer()\n        }\n\n  # Define Mnesia record\n  Record.defrecord(:lease_record,\n    mac_address: nil,\n    ip_address: nil,\n    pool_name: nil,\n    state: :offered,\n    lease_time: 0,\n    expires_at: 0,\n    hostname: nil,\n    client_id: nil,\n    created_at: 0,\n    updated_at: 0\n  )\n\n  @table_name :dhcpv4_leases\n\n  ## Public API\n\n  @doc \"\"\"\n  Initializes the Mnesia schema and creates the leases table.\n\n  ## Options\n\n  - `:storage_type` - `:disc_copies` (default) or `:ram_copies`\n  - `:nodes` - List of nodes to create table on (default: [node()])\n\n  ## Returns\n\n  - `:ok` - Successfully initialized\n  - `{:error, reason}` - Failed to initialize\n  \"\"\"\n  @spec init(keyword()) :: :ok | {:error, term()}\n  def init(opts \\\\ []) do\n    storage_type = Keyword.get(opts, :storage_type, :disc_copies)\n    nodes = Keyword.get(opts, :nodes, [node()])\n\n    with :ok <- ensure_schema_created(nodes),","numLines":80,"startLine":1,"totalLines":639}}}
