{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Hoy6vE9noHAkzmBtKgDr2c","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→defmodule YellowDog.Console.DnsLive.Index do\n     2→  @moduledoc \"\"\"\n     3→  DNS Overview page showing service status, summary statistics, and cache metrics.\n     4→  \"\"\"\n     5→  use YellowDog.Console, :live_view\n     6→\n     7→  alias YellowDog.Dns.View\n     8→\n     9→  @max_cache_entries 10_000\n    10→\n    11→  @impl true\n    12→  def mount(_params, _session, socket) do\n    13→    if connected?(socket) do\n    14→      Phoenix.PubSub.subscribe(YellowDog.Console.PubSub, \"dns:views\")\n    15→      Phoenix.PubSub.subscribe(YellowDog.Console.PubSub, \"dns:zones\")\n    16→      Phoenix.PubSub.subscribe(YellowDog.Console.PubSub, \"dns:cache\")\n    17→    end\n    18→\n    19→    {:ok,\n    20→     socket\n    21→     |> assign(:page_title, \"DNS Overview\")\n    22→     |> assign(:status, get_dns_status())\n    23→     |> assign(:stats, get_dns_stats())\n    24→     |> assign(:cache_stats, get_cache_stats())}\n    25→  end\n    26→\n    27→  @impl true\n    28→  def handle_event(\"refresh\", _params, socket) do\n    29→    {:noreply,\n    30→     socket\n    31→     |> assign(:status, get_dns_status())\n    32→     |> assign(:stats, get_dns_stats())\n    33→     |> assign(:cache_stats, get_cache_stats())}\n    34→  end\n    35→\n    36→  @impl true\n    37→  def handle_info({:view_updated, _view_name}, socket) do\n    38→    {:noreply, assign(socket, :stats, get_dns_stats())}\n    39→  end\n    40→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01PNHHDtBt8jxbNSX5ewiCya","session_id":"0d3ee750-7f11-4e1e-a617-3b37d644afe9","uuid":"b5ef64e7-ffba-46c3-b7aa-f9cf194f8769","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/gao/Workspace/gsmlg-dev/yellow-dog/apps/yellow_dog_console/lib/yellow_dog/console/live/dns_live/index.ex","content":"defmodule YellowDog.Console.DnsLive.Index do\n  @moduledoc \"\"\"\n  DNS Overview page showing service status, summary statistics, and cache metrics.\n  \"\"\"\n  use YellowDog.Console, :live_view\n\n  alias YellowDog.Dns.View\n\n  @max_cache_entries 10_000\n\n  @impl true\n  def mount(_params, _session, socket) do\n    if connected?(socket) do\n      Phoenix.PubSub.subscribe(YellowDog.Console.PubSub, \"dns:views\")\n      Phoenix.PubSub.subscribe(YellowDog.Console.PubSub, \"dns:zones\")\n      Phoenix.PubSub.subscribe(YellowDog.Console.PubSub, \"dns:cache\")\n    end\n\n    {:ok,\n     socket\n     |> assign(:page_title, \"DNS Overview\")\n     |> assign(:status, get_dns_status())\n     |> assign(:stats, get_dns_stats())\n     |> assign(:cache_stats, get_cache_stats())}\n  end\n\n  @impl true\n  def handle_event(\"refresh\", _params, socket) do\n    {:noreply,\n     socket\n     |> assign(:status, get_dns_status())\n     |> assign(:stats, get_dns_stats())\n     |> assign(:cache_stats, get_cache_stats())}\n  end\n\n  @impl true\n  def handle_info({:view_updated, _view_name}, socket) do\n    {:noreply, assign(socket, :stats, get_dns_stats())}\n  end\n","numLines":40,"startLine":1,"totalLines":171}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Cwxk5DUmnDmk4mYhpPQEea","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→defmodule YellowDog.Console.Components.RecordForm do\n     2→  @moduledoc \"\"\"\n     3→  LiveComponent for DNS record editing with real-time validation.\n     4→\n     5→  This component provides:\n     6→  - Type-specific form fields (different fields for MX, SRV, CAA, etc.)\n     7→  - Real-time validation feedback using `phx-change`\n     8→  - Conflict detection warnings (e.g., CNAME at existing name)\n     9→  - Integration with DNS.Zone.Validator.Record for RFC-compliant validation\n    10→\n    11→  ## Usage\n    12→\n    13→      <.live_component\n    14→        module={YellowDog.Console.Components.RecordForm}\n    15→        id=\"record-form\"\n    16→        zone_name=\"example.com\"\n    17→        zone_pid={@zone_pid}\n    18→        record={@editing_record}\n    19→        on_save={fn record -> send(self(), {:record_saved, record}) end}\n    20→        on_cancel={fn -> send(self(), :record_cancelled) end}\n    21→      />\n    22→\n    23→  ## Assigns\n    24→\n    25→  - `:zone_name` - The zone name for relative name resolution\n    26→  - `:zone_pid` - PID of the Auth zone process (optional, for conflict detection)\n    27→  - `:record` - Existing record map for editing, or nil for new record\n    28→  - `:on_save` - Callback function when form is submitted successfully\n    29→  - `:on_cancel` - Callback function when form is cancelled\n    30→\n    31→  \"\"\"\n    32→  use YellowDog.Console, :live_component\n    33→\n    34→  alias DNS.Zone.Validator.Record, as: RecordValidator\n    35→\n    36→  @supported_types ~w(a aaaa cname mx ns txt srv ptr caa)\n    37→\n    38→  # ============================================================================\n    39→  # Lifecycle\n    40→  # ============================================================================\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01PNHHDtBt8jxbNSX5ewiCya","session_id":"0d3ee750-7f11-4e1e-a617-3b37d644afe9","uuid":"f84c21eb-a957-4e87-a8e9-7dbf6614d882","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/gao/Workspace/gsmlg-dev/yellow-dog/apps/yellow_dog_console/lib/yellow_dog/console/components/record_form.ex","content":"defmodule YellowDog.Console.Components.RecordForm do\n  @moduledoc \"\"\"\n  LiveComponent for DNS record editing with real-time validation.\n\n  This component provides:\n  - Type-specific form fields (different fields for MX, SRV, CAA, etc.)\n  - Real-time validation feedback using `phx-change`\n  - Conflict detection warnings (e.g., CNAME at existing name)\n  - Integration with DNS.Zone.Validator.Record for RFC-compliant validation\n\n  ## Usage\n\n      <.live_component\n        module={YellowDog.Console.Components.RecordForm}\n        id=\"record-form\"\n        zone_name=\"example.com\"\n        zone_pid={@zone_pid}\n        record={@editing_record}\n        on_save={fn record -> send(self(), {:record_saved, record}) end}\n        on_cancel={fn -> send(self(), :record_cancelled) end}\n      />\n\n  ## Assigns\n\n  - `:zone_name` - The zone name for relative name resolution\n  - `:zone_pid` - PID of the Auth zone process (optional, for conflict detection)\n  - `:record` - Existing record map for editing, or nil for new record\n  - `:on_save` - Callback function when form is submitted successfully\n  - `:on_cancel` - Callback function when form is cancelled\n\n  \"\"\"\n  use YellowDog.Console, :live_component\n\n  alias DNS.Zone.Validator.Record, as: RecordValidator\n\n  @supported_types ~w(a aaaa cname mx ns txt srv ptr caa)\n\n  # ============================================================================\n  # Lifecycle\n  # ============================================================================","numLines":40,"startLine":1,"totalLines":768}}}
